# base_unittests tests that do not pass on Jam OS yet (tools/cr-test.sh base,
# tools/cr/base-run.py). A "[layer] reason" line, then the full names of the
# tests it explains, one a line (a name may use * as the wildcard). Or one
# line "<pattern> <layer> <reason>". The tests are not run (CR_BASE_ALL=1
# runs them anyway and reports a failure as known), so a `base` PASS means
# every other test passed.
#
# Made 2026-10-16 from CR_BASE_ALL=1 runs of the shards of the suites on
# base_unittests relinked against main's libc (tools/cr/base-run.py: each
# suite a program of its own; tests that crashed alone). The layer is the
# track that owns the fix: posix (libc and its call layer), proc (/proc
# files), fs (a file system under /data: extfs, or the mapping calls),
# launch (starting programs: CB5's launcher patch), jit (executable memory
# by capability), toolchain (the link), musl (musl's own behaviour: the
# same on Linux with musl). A cause marked "?" is a guess from the failing call.
# Findings with their evidence: docs/CR-PLAN.md, "CB2 as built" and "CB2b on ext".
#
# The list is for an ext /data (CB2b, 2026-10-16: the 44 file-system tests that
# only a FAT /data fails are in base_unittests.fat.skip, which base-run.py adds
# when the stick's /data is FAT).

[posix] death tests: gtest makes the test's child with fork() (fast style: syscall 57, ENOSYS, seen with TEST_TMPDIR set) or clone(SIGCHLD) (threadsafe style: gtest-death-test.cc:1329; __jam_clone refuses a process clone with -ENOSYS and no log line), CaptureStderr() has already redirected stderr, so the abort that follows is silent
